      "text": "Our reading corner is small, but it has gradually become one of the most useful spaces in our home. The books are on a low shelf, where my child can reach them without asking for help. We rotate a few titles rather than put every book out at once. This makes choosing easier and sometimes brings forgotten favorites back into view. There is no special rule about how long we must sit there. Some days we read several stories; other days we only look at a few pictures. I have noticed that a comfortable space can make a habit easier to begin. The corner does not make us read automatically, but it removes a few small obstacles that used to get in the way. The environment influences behavior even when we are not consciously thinking about it. Making books visible and easy to reach does not guarantee interest, but it increases the chance that reading will become an ordinary choice rather than a special event.",
