      "text": "Cooking a simple lunch reminds me how many decisions hide inside an ordinary task. I check what we already have before deciding what to make. If there are vegetables left from yesterday, I try to use them instead of letting them go to waste. While the rice cooks, I prepare the rest of the meal. My child stays away from the stove but can help with safe tasks, such as carrying napkins to the table. I describe what I am doing and explain why some things need care. Not every meal turns out as I hoped, and the kitchen is rarely tidy afterward. Still, sharing food that we have prepared gives an everyday task a sense of purpose. Involving a child may reduce efficiency in the short term, yet create opportunities to practice cooperation. The aim is not to make every household task educational. It is to notice when a manageable contribution can help a child feel included in family life.",
