      "text": "A learning habit becomes more useful when I know exactly what I am trying to practice. Simply opening an English app does not guarantee that I will pay attention or remember anything. Before each session, I choose a small task: understand a short recording, retell an experience, or use a new phrase in conversation. Afterward, I check what I can do without looking at the material. This sometimes feels harder than reading the same passage again, but it shows me what I actually remember. I also try to make starting easy by keeping my book and headphones in one place. Motivation changes from day to day. A clear task and a simple routine help me continue when the excitement wears off. Feedback is valuable only if it changes what I do next. Collecting corrections without using them can create the appearance of progress. I therefore choose one recurring problem, practice a better version, and look for an opportunity to use it spontaneously.",
